    fix(daemon): dispatch routed AgentTasks through the cascade coordinator (DF-SPECLANG-015)
    
    The daemon routed spec_writer AgentTasks (emit 'task') but nothing consumed
    them: the only listener logged the task and dropped it, so reactive expansion
    produced no agent session. The recovered watchDaemon() had no caller in any
    production path, and it dropped the executor's stdout, so even a manual call
    could never write its output.
    
    - bin/speclangd: construct a CascadeCoordinator and call
      coordinator.watchDaemon(d, {verbose}) in the foreground start branch — the
      branch the background `-d` child re-executes, so both start modes get the
      watcher; one-shot subcommands (status/pause/stop/...) stay untouched.
      --verbose is forwarded to the spawned child.
    - specs/daemon.spec.dir/src/speclangd.ts: same wiring in the spec-side CLI
      start action, plus a --verbose flag on `start`.
    - coordinator/invocation.ts: InvocationResult gains `output`, and invoke()
      now copies the executor's `output` and `error` through. Judge probe
      d143a7ea showed an executor returning {output:'BODY'} produced
      result.output === undefined, so watchDaemon's write-to-target branch could
      never fire.
    - coordinator/index.ts: use the typed field instead of an `as any` cast.
    - tests/daemon/df-spec-015-watch-daemon.test.ts: output propagation, live
      dispatch + write-to-target, in-flight/TTL dedup, no-trigger skip, and static
      assertions that both daemon entrypoints actually call watchDaemon.
    
    Verified: npm run build exit 0; full suite 1858 passed / 58 skipped; live
    probe against the real speclangd (stub SPECLANG_BIN, no LLM) logged
    "Wrote agent output to generated/probe.spec.md (47 bytes)" with the stub body.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
